    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0724" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0093 D 34/734</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Oudendijk</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Senior Minister, to the American Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>)<anchor n="15" xml:id="d425-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                        1925.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Circular No. 30</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject:—Situation in Shanghai.</p>
                <p>Referring to Circular No. 21<anchor n="16" xml:id="d425-f2"/> the Senior Minister
                    has the honour to circulate herewith among his Honourable Colleagues the
                    translation of a Note, dated February 4th, which he received from the Wai <pb
                        facs="0725" n="599" xml:id="pg599"/> Chiao Pu in reply to his Note of
                    January 27th,<anchor n="16a" xml:id="d425-f3"/> on the subject of the situation
                    in and around Shanghai.</p>
                <p>A copy of this translation has been sent to the Senior Consul in Shanghai.</p>


                <xi:include href="d425-a1.xml" xpointer="d425-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
